{"title":"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">2021 AMC 10A #9</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2021 AMC 12A #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Expand)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Expand)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Expand_and_then_Factor)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Expand and then Factor)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Beyond_Overkill)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Beyond Overkill)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:30)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:30)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Simple_&amp;_Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Simple &amp; Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Aaron_He_(Trivial_Inequality)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Aaron He (Trivial Inequality)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_North_America_Math_Contest_Go_Go_Go_(Trivial_Inequality,_Simon&#39;s_Favourite_Packing_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by North America Math Contest Go Go Go (Trivial Inequality, Simon's Favourite Packing Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Trivial_Inequality,_Simon&#39;s_Favorite_Factoring)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Trivial Inequality, Simon's Favorite Factoring)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Learning_Royal\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Learning Royal</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Yet_another_Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Yet another Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d26eaf1c5b8cf1f23ec4f93b39fa3382eb061724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(xy-1)^2+(x+y)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"19\" /> for real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91ce505bc957f90a725280b7eb2a62929395374d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~0\\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~\\frac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~\\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~1 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"356\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Expand.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Expand)\">Solution 1 (Expand)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Expand)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Expanding, we get that the expression is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce2493f4e36d5332a9b16cc08d5dd1c16dbdd2af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+2xy+y^2+x^2y^2-2xy+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"247\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a0b634e30cf0dd5cf00c723ee1f3fc47ddc2a53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2+x^2y^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />. By the Trivial Inequality (all squares are nonnegative) the minimum value for this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/168a130bed931e0f84853e7de5424269a5a88859.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} ~1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />, which can be achieved at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08cc55a3a19c9f8cf005f17391db8ed355d2909c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>~aop2014\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Expand_and_then_Factor.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Expand_and_then_Factor)\">Solution 2 (Expand and then Factor)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Expand and then Factor)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We expand the original expression, then factor the result by grouping:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d83fdf5482fab294f40a37ffca526aeb1ebde4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (xy-1)^2+(x+y)^2&amp;=\\left(x^2y^2-2xy+1\\right)+\\left(x^2+2xy+y^2\\right) \\\\ &amp;=x^2y^2+x^2+y^2+1 \\\\ &amp;=x^2\\left(y^2+1\\right)+\\left(y^2+1\\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\left(x^2+1\\right)\\left(y^2+1\\right). \\end{align*}\" width=\"459\" height=\"105\" />\nClearly, both factors are positive. By the Trivial Inequality, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8afd2da87874b8455fa5cdce076c030b2796580.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(x^2+1\\right)\\left(y^2+1\\right)\\geq\\left(0+1\\right)\\left(0+1\\right)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} ~1}.\\]\" width=\"350\" height=\"28\" />\nNote that the least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d26eaf1c5b8cf1f23ec4f93b39fa3382eb061724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(xy-1)^2+(x+y)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"19\" /> occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c81b11d933e601724725c8f625d405d76a87fdcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Beyond_Overkill.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Beyond_Overkill)\">Solution 3 (Beyond Overkill)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Beyond Overkill)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like solution 1, expand and simplify the original equation to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a0b634e30cf0dd5cf00c723ee1f3fc47ddc2a53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2+x^2y^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2fa01749b05d8f8e474279c8efeefe5e0d9c610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x, y) = x^2+y^2+x^2y^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"19\" />. To find local extrema, find where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/318e62ee5c32c0384117a780e4caa8dceba95663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nabla f(x, y) = \\boldsymbol{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />. First, find the first partial derivative with respect to x and y and find where they are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c8883627988c35283b34d3dfa17825ed8bf491d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = 2x + 2xy^{2} = 2x(1 + y^{2}) = 0 \\implies x = 0\\]\" width=\"358\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fde4a923b8182ddc56a7bc835d6d6b8a438e351.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y} = 2y + 2yx^{2} = 2y(1 + x^{2}) = 0 \\implies y = 0\\]\" width=\"356\" height=\"42\" />\nThus, there is a local extremum at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Because this is the only extremum, we can assume that this is a minimum because the problem asks for the minimum (though this can also be proven using the partial second derivative test) and the global minimum since it's the only minimum, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0d3df1b7dd74d433aa5c91d5d548a7bcae03759.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> is the minimum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/9166ef883925e9f0447ca79c079786b35ad43671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/9166ef883925e9f0447ca79c079786b35ad43671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, we find 1 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/7/7b790a4d95adb4487e600d15c83bf399e11b7cfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} ~1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"100\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ DBlack2021\n</p><p>Remark:\nHonestly, this isn't even that overkill. I did it this way, and it was not very bashy.\n~vaishnav\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:30.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:30)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:30)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:30)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/4SslunY-b_c\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/4SslunY-b_c</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p><p>Note: the problem where this is linked is covered 0:21-0:50\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Simple_.26_Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Simple_&amp;_Quick)\">Video Solution (Simple &amp; Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Simple &amp; Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2CZ1u4J9yk4\">https://youtu.be/2CZ1u4J9yk4</a>\n</p><p>~ Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Aaron_He_.28Trivial_Inequality.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Aaron_He_(Trivial_Inequality)\">Video Solution by Aaron He (Trivial Inequality)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Aaron He (Trivial Inequality)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xTGDKBthWsw&amp;t=6m58s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xTGDKBthWsw&amp;t=6m58s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_North_America_Math_Contest_Go_Go_Go_.28Trivial_Inequality.2C_Simon.27s_Favourite_Packing_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_North_America_Math_Contest_Go_Go_Go_(Trivial_Inequality,_Simon's_Favourite_Packing_Theorem)\">Video Solution by North America Math Contest Go Go Go (Trivial Inequality, Simon's Favourite Packing Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by North America Math Contest Go Go Go (Trivial Inequality, Simon&#39;s Favourite Packing Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PbJK4KKfQjY&amp;list=PLexHyfQ8DMuKqltG3cHT7Di4jhVl6L4YJ&amp;index=8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PbJK4KKfQjY&amp;list=PLexHyfQ8DMuKqltG3cHT7Di4jhVl6L4YJ&amp;index=8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Hawk Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P5al76DxyHY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P5al76DxyHY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Trivial_Inequality.2C_Simon.27s_Favorite_Factoring.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Trivial_Inequality,_Simon's_Favorite_Factoring)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Trivial Inequality, Simon's Favorite Factoring)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Trivial Inequality, Simon&#39;s Favorite Factoring)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DP0ppuQzFPE\">https://youtu.be/DP0ppuQzFPE</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_6\">Video Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hmOGYmVmY1c\">https://youtu.be/hmOGYmVmY1c</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/s6E4E06XhPU?t=640\">https://youtu.be/s6E4E06XhPU?t=640</a> (for AMC 10A)\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/cckGBU2x1zg?t=95\">https://youtu.be/cckGBU2x1zg?t=95</a> (for AMC 12A)\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Learning_Royal\">Video Solution by The Learning Royal</span><span class=\"mw-edit